const e="srs-bsme-art-competition",d=2025,t="Read from the SRS BSME Art Competition 2024-2025 rules PDF (11 pages). No entry fee, venue address or named contact person is printed; the organiser's contact page is the only contact. Prize amounts are not printed. The rules print two judging tables; both are recorded in the text and the template uses the main one. The application form is mainly for People of Determination entries; its parent and teacher phone, address and signature fields are described, not copied.",n={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"SRS BSME Art Competition - a project of Research Science Investment",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"Registration opens {{RegistrationOpens}} and closes {{RegistrationCloses}}. Artwork submission deadline: {{SubmissionDeadline}}. Theme: {{Theme}}.",Notes:["Teachers submit the students' artwork online and agree to the competition terms on the organiser's platform.","The judges' rulings are final and without appeal.","Prizes are for individual work; group work cannot enter."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General",Items:["Goals: to encourage student creativity, to increase artistic awareness in schools, and to enable talented students to communicate through the field of art.","The theme for the year is {{Theme}}. Students produce their own artwork on the given theme.","Entries must be a drawing, painting, photograph or digital art. Three dimensional sculptures are not accepted.","Entries can use any traditional medium, including pastel, oil pastel, pen, pencil, charcoal, acrylics, watercolour, mixed media or collage, as well as photography and digital art.","The competition takes place at each BSME member school, in suitable premises, with all the materials students ask for provided by the school.","The school competition lasts a maximum of 2 hours.","Schools must provide photographic or video evidence, taken in the classroom or at the area the school has set, to show the integrity of the competition.","Submitted artwork must be the student's own original creation. An exact copy of an existing image, visually or by tracing, is not acceptable. The organiser disqualifies a work it reasonably suspects is wholly copied.","Adults may give encouragement but must not have a hands-on role in creating the artwork.","Do not submit: blurry images, low resolution images, images under 2000 px on the widest edge, Google or stock images, or Artificial Intelligence (AI) images or artworks.","The organiser may reject entries it considers inappropriate for any reason. It can publish or decline to publish, and use or decline to use, any submitted artwork at its sole discretion.","The organiser may crop or correct artwork for display and to keep the display consistent.","The organiser may change, cancel or suspend the competition, or any part of it, if outside circumstances arise that it cannot reasonably control. The competition runs under these rules, which the organiser may amend."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Who may enter",Items:["Students of BSME member schools in the year groups 5-6, 7-9, 10-11 and 12-13.","Only individual work may enter. Group work cannot enter.","Teachers must submit their students' artwork and agree to the terms and conditions on the organiser's online platform.","The organiser can ask a contestant for a copy of a birth certificate, a parent's ID or other proof of age.","The People of Determination application form asks for: the name, age and kind of disability (People of Determination, hearing impairment, sight impairment, autism, Down syndrome or any other), the child's and the school's details, parent or guardian and teacher names, phone numbers, mobile numbers, e-mails and signatures, and a school holiday contact. Entries for children under 18 must be signed by an adult.","The form lists the categories Child 7-15 years and Youth 16-18, and the three art types: Drawing and Painting, Digital Art, Photography."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to enter",Items:["Register on the organiser's website during the registration period ({{RegistrationOpens}} to {{RegistrationCloses}}).","The teacher sends clear digital copies of the artwork, no more than 4 MB each, from scans or photographs, through the teacher's online account on the website. Only the teacher may submit.","Teachers upload the progress evidence together with the final artwork.","Mark each painting or drawing clearly with the student's full name, age, class, city, country and nationality.","By entering, parents and teachers agree that the children's names and artworks appear online and at the exhibition.","By entering, parents and teachers agree that the organiser may use the artwork in merchandise, advertisements, educational materials or publicity without further notice or payment. The contestant keeps the right to use and publish the artwork.","Submission deadline: {{SubmissionDeadline}}.","Questions not answered in the rules: use the organiser's contact page ({{ContactPage}}).","Please tag the organiser on the school's social media pages and use the competition hashtags ({{Hashtags}})."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Provisional schedule",Items:["Registration opens: {{RegistrationOpens}}.","Registration closes: {{RegistrationCloses}}.","Submission deadline: {{SubmissionDeadline}}.","Judging: {{JudgingDate}}.","Winner announcement: {{WinnerAnnouncement}}."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging",Items:["The judges' rulings are final and without appeal in all matters related to the competition and the awarding of prizes.","Judging criteria, out of 100: Creative Thinking 25, Using materials in an efficient way 25, Clarity of idea in the completed work 25, Quality of final work 25.","The application-form page prints a second set of criteria, out of 100: Creative Thinking 20, Efficiently using materials 20, The clarity of an idea 20, Emotion in art 20, Quality of process and the final outcome 20. The document does not say which set is used for which art type."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Prizes and awards",Items:["Prizes are given for the winner and the runner up of each year group (5 to 13).","Additional prizes and commendations may be given for artworks.","Individual prizes may include cash, gift vouchers or other prizes. {{Prizes}}","Cash prizes are offered, and the parent's ID is requested to check and start the prize giving.","Winners are acknowledged on the organiser's website and social media.","After the winners are announced, students have 30 days to claim their prizes and are told the steps and requirements. If the deadlines the organiser announces are missed, the organiser has no responsibility to provide the prizes.","The organiser gives certificates to all participants who make a submission.","Winners are shown on the RSI Art Award and BSME websites and social media through the year.","The organiser may ask schools to send selected original artworks."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Privacy",Items:["The organiser keeps a strict privacy policy and does not share entrants' personal data with any other party without the consent of the parent or teacher.","It collects personal information for registration, programme evaluation and keeping entrants informed, and may contact winners and runners up for ID."]}],Documents:[{Title:"SRS BSME Art Competition rules 2024-2025 (PDF)",Url:"https://rsiartaward.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/SRS-BSME-Art-Competition-Rules-Sep-2024-2025.pdf"}]},a=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Rules p.5",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Prizes are awarded for individual work and not for group projects. Group work cannot enter."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- Prizes are awarded for individual work and not for group projects. Group work cannot enter.`}],o=[],i=[{Title:"Drawing and Painting",Source:"Rules p.2, p.4",Sections:{About:["Submissions can be paintings or drawings in any medium, including crayons, watercolours or acrylic."],TimeAndFormat:["The school competition lasts a maximum of 2 hours.","Each entry must be not smaller than A3 (42 x 29.7 cm) and up to A2 (42 x 59.4 cm) paper."],Rules:["Students produce their own artwork on the theme {{Theme}}.","Mark every painting or drawing with the student's full name, age, class, city, country and nationality.","To show the students did the work themselves, teachers submit six (6) photographs of the progress of the work at different stages and upload them with the final outcome.","Samples of dos and don'ts are on the competition website."],Allowed:["Any medium, including crayons, watercolours, acrylic, pastel, oil pastel, pen, pencil, charcoal, mixed media and collage."],NotAllowed:["Exact copies of existing images, tracing, adults working hands-on, and AI images."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Submissions can be paintings or drawings in any medium, including crayons, watercolours or acrylic.

## Time and format
- The school competition lasts a maximum of 2 hours.
- Each entry must be not smaller than A3 (42 x 29.7 cm) and up to A2 (42 x 59.4 cm) paper.

## Rules
- Students produce their own artwork on the theme {{Theme}}.
- Mark every painting or drawing with the student's full name, age, class, city, country and nationality.
- To show the students did the work themselves, teachers submit six (6) photographs of the progress of the work at different stages and upload them with the final outcome.
- Samples of dos and don'ts are on the competition website.

## Allowed
- Any medium, including crayons, watercolours, acrylic, pastel, oil pastel, pen, pencil, charcoal, mixed media and collage.

## Not allowed
- Exact copies of existing images, tracing, adults working hands-on, and AI images.`},{Title:"Digital Art",Source:"Rules p.3",Sections:{About:["Original digital artwork created by students."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["Artwork must be original and created by students.","File format JPG, 300 DPI, highest compression quality of 12.","At least 2480 px on the longest edge and not more than 4 MB.","Artwork must be clear and in focus.","Any app can be used (Photoshop, Illustrator, Procreate, Artrage and others)."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["Frames, mats or watermarks.","Artificial Intelligence (AI) images or artworks."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Original digital artwork created by students.

## Rules
- Artwork must be original and created by students.
- File format JPG, 300 DPI, highest compression quality of 12.
- At least 2480 px on the longest edge and not more than 4 MB.
- Artwork must be clear and in focus.
- Any app can be used (Photoshop, Illustrator, Procreate, Artrage and others).

## Not allowed
- Frames, mats or watermarks.
- Artificial Intelligence (AI) images or artworks.`},{Title:"Photography",Source:"Rules p.3",Sections:{About:["Photographs taken by students."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["All photographs must be 30 x 40 cm.","Only 2 images from each participant are accepted."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:["Blurry or low resolution images, images under 2000 px on the widest edge, Google or stock images, and AI images."],Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Photographs taken by students.

## Rules
- All photographs must be 30 x 40 cm.
- Only 2 images from each participant are accepted.

## Not allowed
- Blurry or low resolution images, images under 2000 px on the widest edge, Google or stock images, and AI images.`}],r=[],s=[{Key:"Theme",Kind:"text",Label:"Competition theme",Value:"Future Me",Source:"Rules p.1"},{Key:"RegistrationOpens",Kind:"date",Label:"Registration opens",Value:"2024-09-16",Source:"Rules p.6"},{Key:"RegistrationCloses",Kind:"date",Label:"Registration closes",Value:"2024-11-28",Source:"Rules p.6"},{Key:"SubmissionDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Submission deadline",Value:"2025-01-28",Source:"Rules p.6"},{Key:"JudgingDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Judging",Value:"2025-02-28",Source:"Rules p.6"},{Key:"WinnerAnnouncement",Kind:"date",Label:"Winner announcement",Value:"2025-04-28",Source:"Rules p.6"},{Key:"Prizes",Kind:"prize",Label:"Prizes",Value:"Prizes for the winner and the runner up of each year group; the amounts are not printed.",Source:"Rules p.5"},{Key:"ContactPage",Kind:"link",Label:"Organiser contact page",Value:"https://rsiartaward.com/contact/",Source:"Rules p.5"},{Key:"Hashtags",Kind:"text",Label:"Competition hashtags and social pages",Value:"#SRSBSMEArtCompetition2024_2025 #School_of_Research_Science #BSME #RSI_Art_Award #Art_Competition #Future_Me; pages: School of Research Science and RSI Art Award on Facebook, Instagram and X",Source:"Rules p.11"}],l=[{Claim:"SRS BSME Art Competition 2024-2025 rules.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"SRS BSME Art Competition 2024-2025 rules",Url:"https://rsiartaward.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/SRS-BSME-Art-Competition-Rules-Sep-2024-2025.pdf"}],c={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:t,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:a,AgeGroups:o,Competitions:i,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{o as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,i as Competitions,l as Evidence,t as Note,n as Page,a as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,d as Year,c as default};
